From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fix <fix@example.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Mar 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] xone-wired: Fix USB reset race condition causing system
 freeze

The xone_wired driver was calling usb_reset_device() unconditionally
in probe(), which causes severe race conditions when the controller is
rapidly connected/disconnected. This can leave the xHCI controller in
a bad state, eventually causing a complete system freeze.

The reset was intended for "newer devices after system sleep" but was
being applied to all connections. This is the same bug that was already
fixed in the dongle driver (see dongle.c:1495-1499).

The fix:
1. Remove the unconditional usb_reset_device() from probe
2. Add proper reset_resume handler that reinitializes the device after
   system resume, similar to how the dongle driver handles it

This allows rapid plug/unplug operations without freezing the system,
while still properly handling resume from sleep.

Fixes: https://github.com/dlundqvist/xone/issues/14
---
 transport/wired.c | 55 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 50 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/transport/wired.c b/transport/wired.c
index 0000000..1111111 100644
--- a/transport/wired.c
+++ b/transport/wired.c
@@ -482,9 +482,6 @@ static int xone_wired_probe(struct usb_interface *intf,

 	wired->udev = interface_to_usbdev(intf);

-	/* newer devices require a reset after system sleep */
-	usb_reset_device(wired->udev);
-
 	err = xone_wired_init_data_port(wired, intf);
 	if (err)
 		return err;
@@ -542,6 +539,53 @@ static void xone_wired_disconnect(struct usb_interface *intf)
 	usb_set_intfdata(intf, NULL);
 }

+static int xone_wired_suspend(struct usb_interface *intf, pm_message_t message)
+{
+	struct xone_wired *wired = usb_get_intfdata(intf);
+
+	/* ignore audio interface */
+	if (!wired)
+		return 0;
+
+	usb_kill_urb(wired->data_port.urb_in);
+	usb_kill_urb(wired->audio_port.urb_in);
+	usb_kill_anchored_urbs(&wired->data_port.urbs_out_busy);
+	usb_kill_anchored_urbs(&wired->audio_port.urbs_out_busy);
+
+	return 0;
+}
+
+static int xone_wired_resume(struct usb_interface *intf)
+{
+	struct xone_wired *wired = usb_get_intfdata(intf);
+	int err;
+
+	/* ignore audio interface */
+	if (!wired)
+		return 0;
+
+	/* restart data input */
+	err = usb_submit_urb(wired->data_port.urb_in, GFP_KERNEL);
+	if (err)
+		return err;
+
+	/* restart audio input if it was active */
+	if (wired->audio_port.urb_in) {
+		err = usb_submit_urb(wired->audio_port.urb_in, GFP_KERNEL);
+		if (err)
+			return err;
+	}
+
+	return 0;
+}
+
+static int xone_wired_reset_resume(struct usb_interface *intf)
+{
+	/* The kernel already reset the device before calling reset_resume.
+	 * Just resume normally without an additional reset. */
+	return xone_wired_resume(intf);
+}
+
 static const struct usb_device_id xone_wired_id_table[] = {
 	{ XONE_WIRED_VENDOR(0x045e) }, /* Microsoft */
 	{ XONE_WIRED_VENDOR(0x0738) }, /* Mad Catz */
@@ -573,6 +617,9 @@ static struct usb_driver xone_wired_driver = {
 	.probe = xone_wired_probe,
 	.disconnect = xone_wired_disconnect,
 	.id_table = xone_wired_id_table,
+	.suspend = xone_wired_suspend,
+	.resume = xone_wired_resume,
+	.reset_resume = xone_wired_reset_resume,
 };

 module_usb_driver(xone_wired_driver);
--
2.46.0
